meta {
  name: 07 Expedited screening — contract-exact household-only
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/eligibility/evaluate/expedited-screening
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "metadata": {},
    "household": { "size": 1, "housingCosts": 800, "utilityCosts": 150 }
  }
}

docs {
  The contract-exact shape: household only, no members. The published
  household object carries no income or liquid-resource fields, so the
  273.2(i) comparison (income + resources vs. shelter costs) cannot
  actually be computed from it.

  Expected: a conservative { "expedited": false } plus
  x-missingInformation listing what would be needed — rather than a 400,
  and rather than presenting an unknown as a confident "no". This is
  finding #1 in docs/v1-conformance.md.
}
